{
  "_comment": "The vessels the tracker draws. Positions are not stored: src/utils/fleet.js works each one out from the wall clock, so the map moves on its own and never goes stale. `route` is the ordered track, built from ports and from the sea waypoints below \u2014 a great circle straight from one port to the next sails over continents, so every leg is short enough to be honest water. `calls` is the subset where cargo is actually worked. A voyage takes as long as its route and the vessel's service speed say it does, so the speed on screen is the speed the marker travels, plus a turnaround alongside (turnaroundDays); `phase` spreads the fleet across that cycle. To drive this from a live AIS feed instead, replace the body of fleet.readFleet(): the shape it returns is the contract.",
